s governed by separate instructions?","After 30 November 2024, are existing channels unavailable in all cases, or can IPD authorize an exception?","Is recurring annual-fee settlement merely an optional facility, or is it mandatory for specified products under another instrument?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["“Investment products administered by IPD” is limited to products within the categories listed in footnote 1.","The transition date is interpreted by calendar date in Hong Kong without an unstated time-of-day rule.","The phrase “can also settle” is permissive and does not expand the compulsory submission duty."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"u4"},{"quote":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"u9"}],"distinction":"Primary reading: the parallel run ends at the close of 29 November 2024, and from 30 November 2024 every covered IPD application or submission must use e-IP. Existing channels are accepted only during the parallel run. Recurring annual-fee settlement is an additional available function, not itself a compulsory filing route.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The selected filing is an application or submission of an investment product administered by IPD.","name":"covered_ipd_filing","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9","u17"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The filing date is on or after the compu